<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" version="2.0"><channel><title>Kramer Elementary School News</title><link>https://www.talawanda.org/</link><description>News and announcements from Kramer Elementary School, including events, activities, and important dates.</description><docs>http://www.rssboard.org/rss-specification</docs><generator>Talawanda Enews RSS Converter</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 05 May 2026 19:21:10 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>City of Oxford Parks Master Plan Survey</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/2d7rz#b4a0e3l66z</link><description>&lt;p&gt;The City of Oxford is developing a Parks Master Plan with Pros Consulting and is seeking feedback from Talawanda families who use the parks. Residents can participate by completing a &lt;strong&gt;survey, virtual mapping exercise, and vision board&lt;/strong&gt; at the dedicated website: https://engagepros.mysocialpinpoint.com/oxford&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/2d7rz#b4a0e3l66z"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">b4a0e3l66z</guid><pubDate>Fri, 01 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Connect Kroger Rewards to Kramer PTG</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/2d7rz#bncw8zzi9l</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Link your Kroger Rewards card to Kramer PTG&lt;/strong&gt; to help support the school. When you shop at Kroger, a percentage of your purchase is donated to the PTG at no cost to you. Each account can only be connected to one nonprofit, and you only need to sign up once. &lt;a href="https://www.kroger.com/i/community/community-rewards"&gt;Sign up here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/2d7rz#bncw8zzi9l"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bncw8zzi9l</guid><pubDate>Fri, 01 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Kramer Reading at Home Program Success</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/2d7rz#bsddobrcr6</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Kramer's Reading at Home (RAH) program achieved remarkable participation this year, with &lt;strong&gt;82% of K-2 students (208 readers)&lt;/strong&gt; turning in at least one reading sheet. Nearly half submitted 10+ sheets, while &lt;strong&gt;26 students read over 500 books&lt;/strong&gt; and three students each read more than &lt;strong&gt;1,000 books&lt;/strong&gt;. Students collectively recorded &lt;strong&gt;over 39,000 books read&lt;/strong&gt; and took home 1,000+ books from the RAH cart. Popular rewards included coupons to Oxford Doughnut Shoppe and Spring Street Treats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/2d7rz#bsddobrcr6"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bsddobrcr6-bsxiwu3i6i-buuj5bybgo-b6gerqak7c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 01 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Kramer Mile Fundraiser - May 11th</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/2d7rz#b5m8132v16</link><description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Kramer Mile fundraiser is on May 11th&lt;/strong&gt; with each grade level running together down Sycamore Street. Students are encouraged to set up fundraising pages at &lt;a href="https://app.99pledges.com/fund/kramermile26/addme"&gt;https://app.99pledges.com/fund/kramermile26/addme&lt;/a&gt; to collect donations (online until midnight May 10th, or cash/check). The grade level raising the most money wins an ice cream party, and top three individual fundraisers win prize packs. Family and friends can run with students or cheer them on. Donations support PTG funding for field trips, assemblies, and classroom materials.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Add to Calendar:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?action=TEMPLATE&amp;text=Kramer%20Mile%20Fundraiser&amp;dates=20260511T000000/20260511T010000&amp;details=The%20%2A%2AKramer%20Mile%20fundraiser%20is%20on%20May%2011th%2A%2A%20with%20each%20grade%20level%20running%20together%20down%20Sycamore%20Street.%20Students%20are%20encouraged%20to%20set%20up%20fundraising%20pages%20at%20%5Bhttps%3A//app.99pledges.com/fund/kramer&amp;location=Sycamore%20Street%20adjacent%20to%20Kramer%20Elementary"&gt;Google Calendar&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="data:text/calendar;charset=utf-8,BEGIN%3AVCALENDAR%0AVERSION%3A2.0%0ABEGIN%3AVEVENT%0ADTSTART%3A20260511T000000%0ADTEND%3A20260511T010000%0ASUMMARY%3AKramer%20Mile%20Fundraiser%0ADESCRIPTION%3AThe%20%2A%2AKramer%20Mile%20fundraiser%20is%20on%20May%2011th%2A%2A%20with%20each%20grade%20level%20running%20together%20down%20Sycamore%20Street.%20Students%20are%20encouraged%20to%20set%20up%20fundraising%20pages%20at%20%5Bhttps%3A//app.99pledges.com/fund/kramer%0ALOCATION%3ASycamore%20Street%20adjacent%20to%20Kramer%20Elementary%0AEND%3AVEVENT%0AEND%3AVCALENDAR"&gt;iCal&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://outlook.live.com/calendar/0/deeplink/compose?subject=Kramer%20Mile%20Fundraiser&amp;startdt=20260511T000000&amp;enddt=20260511T010000&amp;body=The%20%2A%2AKramer%20Mile%20fundraiser%20is%20on%20May%2011th%2A%2A%20with%20each%20grade%20level%20running%20together%20down%20Sycamore%20Street.%20Students%20are%20encouraged%20to%20set%20up%20fundraising%20pages%20at%20%5Bhttps%3A//app.99pledges.com/fund/kramer&amp;location=Sycamore%20Street%20adjacent%20to%20Kramer%20Elementary"&gt;Outlook&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/2d7rz#b5m8132v16"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">b5m8132v16-by355f6uba-bvfcfqqglt</guid><pubDate>Fri, 01 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Field Day, No School Days, and Recent Activities</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/2d7rz#bmz9zvnn32</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No school Monday, May 4th and Tuesday, May 5th.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Field Day is scheduled for May 8th&lt;/strong&gt; and volunteers are needed—sign up using the QR code or link on the flyer. All parents/guardians must have a background check on file with the board office to attend field trips (processing takes a few days). Recent highlights include 3rd and 5th graders completing testing, 1st graders painting ceramic tiles at You're Fired, 5th graders walking to Spring Street Treats for ice cream, and Kindergarteners visiting Farbach-Werner Nature Preserve.&lt;/p&gt;
