&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/bsdgk#bdq844nase"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bdq844nase-bbh9xjslrg-b6jxf1vp8d-bgfxt1k9q6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Vehicle Line Gates Open at 3:40 PM</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/bsdgk#bf2gr3k7s7</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Due to warmer weather, the blacktop area will be used for afternoon recess and &lt;strong&gt;gates will be closed until 3:40 PM&lt;/strong&gt; for vehicle pickup. The parking lot remains &lt;strong&gt;reserved for staff and Preschool pick-up only&lt;/strong&gt;. Only vehicles displaying the &lt;strong&gt;orange PRESCHOOL sheet&lt;/strong&gt; are permitted in the upper lot during drop-off and pick-up times. Contact the office with any questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/bsdgk#bf2gr3k7s7"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">bf2gr3k7s7-b9kaf6o2mz-botge4f0v3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Read At Home Program and Kroger Rewards</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/e0yz7#b4qrzpzg5c</link><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Read At Home (RAH)&lt;/strong&gt; is a voluntary program for K-2nd grade students at Kramer Elementary that encourages reading at home. Students record books they've read each week on a record sheet and turn it in for rewards, which alternate between a student-selected book and a small prize.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kroger Community Rewards:&lt;/strong&gt; Connect your Kroger Rewards card to Kramer PTG (one nonprofit per account) and Kroger will donate a percentage of your purchases to the PTG. Sign up once at https://www.kroger.com/i/community/community-rewards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/e0yz7#b4qrzpzg5c"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">b4qrzpzg5c-bwulg9ornb-bncw8zzi9l</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Kramer Free Pantry Available to Students</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/e0yz7#blqwkxb9tq</link><description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Kramer Free Pantry&lt;/strong&gt; is located at the entrance of Kramer and provides free food and hygiene items to all students. Available items include cereal, fruit, vegetables, peanut butter, spaghetti, mac and cheese, soup, shampoo, and toothbrushes. For questions, donations, or suggestions, contact &lt;strong&gt;Chelsea Pike, Kramer Social Worker&lt;/strong&gt; at &lt;strong&gt;513-273-3511&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;pikec@talawanda.org&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/e0yz7#blqwkxb9tq"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">blqwkxb9tq-brwujkaymx-bx576e3ldv</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Reading Corner Newsletter on Decoding Skills</title><link>https://app.smore.com/n/e0yz7#ber66w8386</link><description>&lt;p&gt;The February &lt;strong&gt;Reading Corner Newsletter&lt;/strong&gt; explains decoding—the foundational reading skill of recognizing letter sounds and blending them to read words. The newsletter provides &lt;strong&gt;grade-specific decoding activities&lt;/strong&gt; for Kindergarten through 3rd grade via Reading Rockets website links, including a video showing how 3rd graders use syllables to decode longer words. Parents can contact Mrs. Geshan (geshanc@talawanda.org), Mrs. Kobermann (kobermanc@talawanda.org), or Mrs. Walters (waltersh@talawanda.org) with questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://app.smore.com/n/e0yz7#ber66w8386"&gt;View original newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">ber66w8386-bn2pap4gkq</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate></item></channel></rss>